{"id": "ae92fa98-1236-4e0f-af82-9444823d020b", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T16:24:19.438502", "source": "agent", "parent_id": null, "system_prompt": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "Collaborate with the researcher to develop an experiment design for the original task. First inspect the masked repository and supplied inputs, then use end_researcher_turn with stage=plan to propose an approach, consequential choices and uncertainties. Wait for explicit researcher approval before developing the full design. After approval, hand off stage=result with the complete design in answer, supported by rationale, controls, feasible checks and repository observations in evidence. State assumptions separately from fixed task requirements. No executed experiment or invented outcome is required for this design-only task. Use inspect_repository and execute_check for exploration. Share concrete findings: private tool output is not automatically sent to the researcher. Revise when needed; do not invent objections or ambiguities to extend the conversation. The researcher decides when to stop."}, "tools": [{"description": "List a repository directory or read a text file. Paths are relative to the task workspace.", "action_type": "InspectRepositoryAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "InspectRepositoryTool", "title": "inspect_repository"}, {"description": "Run a shell command in the isolated task workspace. Use small exploratory checks before submitting your plan.", "action_type": "ExecuteCheckAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ExecuteCheckTool", "title": "execute_check"}, {"description": "Yield a proposed approach (stage=plan) or completed experiment design (stage=result), with evidence, assumptions and uncertainties. The researcher decides when to finish.", "action_type": "ReviewHandoffAction", "observation_type": "BenchmarkObservation", "annotations": null, "meta": null, "kind": "ReviewHandoffTool", "title": "end_researcher_turn"}], "dynamic_context": {"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "<CURRENT_DATETIME>\nThe current date and time is: 2026-10-22T16:24\n</CURRENT_DATETIME>"}, "kind": "SystemPromptEvent"}
{"id": "95ff1d2c-1f5b-4b96-9dbe-f292893d6caa", "timestamp": "2026-10-22T16:24:19.440114", "source": "user", "parent_id": "ae92fa98-1236-4e0f-af82-9444823d020b", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"Okay, before we build anything, let's do a small, bounded pass — no solution yet, just inspection plus a plan.\\n\\n1) Inspection only:\\n   a. List what is actually in /workspace. If Docta source, a package, a README, or an examples/ folder exists, report its real name, version and entry points (e.g. is it a CLI, a Python API, a rule/motif miner, an LLM-style assistant?). I do not want guesses about Docta's interface.\\n   b. Confirm whether any tabular dataset is present anywhere (even a toy CSV), or whether the repositories are truly empty per track.md.\\n   c. Report python3 version and whether any relevant packages are importable. Note: the brief says project dependencies are not preinstalled and network is disabled, so if Docta is not vendored locally, say so plainly rather than papering over it.\\n\\n2) Then return a PROPOSED approach for the design-only deliverable, no more:\\n   - The rare-pattern task definition: what counts as \\\"rare\\\" (support threshold, e.g. fraction of rows), what counts as a \\\"pattern\\\" (conjunction of column predicates, k-mers/episodes, clusters, outliers), and how ground truth rarity is defined so the evaluation is honest.\\n   - Data construction plan: synthetic tabular tables with planted rare patterns (planted conjunctions, perturbed/duplicated rows, controlled noise columns) with controllable rarity and signal strength, plus at least one realistic-shaped control table.\\n   - Detection pipeline with Docta stated as the detector, plus the comparator baselines you would use.\\n   - Metrics, controls and ablations, and a feasibility statement given no compute and no execution.\\n\\n3) List the consequential assumptions and open questions you are making. Specifically flag as unknown, not as fact: which Docta this is, the runtime/resource budget, and the table shape (number of rows/columns, column types, categorical vs numeric, class label present or not). If you must assume something to proceed, label it explicitly as an assumption.\\n\\nKeep it tight and concrete. I want to see the control logic, not a sales pitch.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How can you identify rare patterns in a tabular dataset using Docta?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 224, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null, "reasoning_content": null, "thinking_blocks": [], "responses_reasoning_item": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "critic_result": null, "kind": "MessageEvent"}
